  "slug": "dark-matter-scattering-dce0",
  "summary": "Existing axion and dark-photon cavity experiments can probe millicharged dark matter, while new Casimir proposals target axion-mediated spin forces.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a dominant thread: laboratory detectors designed for light, weakly coupled particles, with axions and dark photons as reference targets. The cavity study shows that resonant microwave cavities built for axion and dark-photon searches can probe ultralight millicharged dark matter through TE modes. The Casimir proposal extends the axion search to spin-dependent interactions, using reversed polarization of magnetically compensated sources to access axion-mediated spin forces. The cost-optimization paper addresses the QCD axion with mass between 10^-11 and 10^-8 eV, motivated by grand unification and string theory, and focuses on detector design economics. What is new is the reuse of established apparatus for dark matter candidates beyond the canonical axion, combined with explicit attention to cost optimization of the detectors themselves.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
